-- Vendors: a catalogue of products from vendors, kept by staff who are each
-- assigned to some of the vendors. The tenth Velle spec, written to exercise
-- the read side of authorization end to end (Reference §22, "The actor"):
-- who may see which records, and which fields of them, applied by the read
-- surface and never inside evaluation.
--
-- What the domain asks of the language, and where each answer lives:
--   · a staff member sees the products of the vendors they are assigned to —
--     a record-level `visible to` clause whose predicate reads the data
--     graph with the viewer bound as `actor`
--   · an administrator sees every product, and alone sees what a product
--     cost — a second record clause, and a field-level clause on `cost`
--   · a vendor's name is public — `visible to anyone`
--   · everything else is staff business — the spec-wide default at the top,
--     which a shape's own clauses replace rather than add to
--   · the margin is calculated from the cost for everyone, whoever asks, and
--     so the margin carries its own clause — the leak through a derivation
--     is the author's to close, never the evaluator's to guess at
--   · a price change below cost is refused, and the refusal handed back to a
--     staff member names the product without its cost — a rejection is
--     projected for the actor as a read is
--
-- Comment convention (as in payments.velle): plain comments tell the business
-- story; `velle:` comments note the language machinery on show.

-- velle: the spec-wide default — every readable shape without a clause of its
-- own is shown to staff and to nobody else
visible to Staff

-- ── People ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- Everyone who keeps the catalogue is staff; administrators also assign
-- vendors and list products. Staff records are seeded by the engineer
-- outside the trust boundary (fixtures, a migration): nothing here hires.
shape Staff {
    name: text
    role: text
}

Staff requires role == "staff" or role == "admin"

shape Administrator = Staff where role == "admin"

-- A staff member is assigned to vendors by an administrator.
shape VendorAssignment {
    staff: one Staff
    vendor: one Vendor
}

transient act AssignVendor by Administrator {
    staff: one Staff
    vendor: one Vendor
}

rule RecordAssignment when AssignVendor {
    VendorAssignment from { staff: staff, vendor: vendor }
}

-- ── Vendors and products ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- velle: `visible to anyone` — a vendor's name is shown to every viewer the
-- binding provides; the clause replaces the spec-wide default for this shape
shape Vendor {
    name: text
    visible to anyone
}

-- A product belongs to a vendor and has a price and a cost. Staff assigned to
-- the vendor see it; administrators see every product and alone see the cost.
-- velle: two record-level clauses disjoin; the field-level clause on `cost`
-- narrows within the record's; `margin` is calculated from `cost` on every
-- read whoever asks, so it carries its own clause
shape Product {
    vendor: one Vendor
    name: text
    price: decimal
    cost: decimal visible to Administrator
    margin: decimal = price - cost visible to Administrator
    visible to Staff where exists (VendorAssignment where staff == actor and vendor == this.vendor)
    visible to Administrator
}

shape ThinMargin = Product where margin < 1.00

transient act ListProduct by Administrator {
    vendor: one Vendor
    name: text
    price: decimal
    cost: decimal
}

rule RecordProduct when ListProduct {
    Product from { vendor: vendor, name: name, price: price, cost: cost }
}

-- A staff member assigned to the vendor may change a product's price, never
-- to below its cost.
-- velle: the gate reads the actor through the data graph (`this.actor` inside
-- the nested `where`, where bare names resolve against the assignment); the
-- prohibition reads a cost the staff member may not see, and refuses all the same
transient act ChangePrice by Staff {
    product: one Product
    price: decimal
}

ChangePrice requires exists (VendorAssignment where staff == this.actor and vendor == this.product.vendor)
never (ChangePrice where price < product.cost)

rule ApplyPrice when ChangePrice {
    product.price = price
}

-- A product whose margin falls under a dollar is flagged once.
-- velle: a rule reading the cost through `margin` for every product — no
-- viewer anywhere in evaluation
shape MarginAlert {
    product: one Product
    raisedOn: timestamp on create
}

rule FlagThinMargin when (ThinMargin where not exists MarginAlert for this) {
    MarginAlert from { product: this }
}
